    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d556-a1">

                <pb facs="0781" n="761" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg761"/>

                <head>Mr. Fessenden to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Department,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-10-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 29, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to state, that on the
                    receipt of your letter of 13th instant covering a copy of the note of J. Hume
                    Burnley, esq., of the British legation, relative to the case of Darrell &amp;
                    Nash, this question was again submitted to the collector at New York for
                    consideration and report, of which report I send you enclosed a copy.</p>
                <p>In view of the facts as stated, I approve his action in the premises, and the
                    same course would have been pursued against the citizens of the United
                    States.</p>
                <p>With great respect,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. P. FESSENDEN, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of
                        Treasury.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d556-a1-a1.xml" xpointer="d556-a1-a1"/>
